From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:13:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6351-fuel-gauge: log each OCV reading

The counted capacity starts from an OCV reading and takes a new one after
a rest. On one boot the starting reading came out about 11 points below
what the charging voltage gave later, and nothing showed what it had
used. Log each reading, first or after a rest, with the open-circuit
voltage, the window current, the temperature and the capacity, at debug
level.
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
index 173f30e..090492f 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
@@ -269,6 +269,8 @@ static int mt6351_fg_capacity(struct mt6351_fg *fg, int ua, int *capacity)
 			*capacity = ret;
 			return 0;
 		}
+		dev_dbg(fg->dev, "%s OCV reading: %d uV at %d uA, %d mC: %d %%\n",
+			fg->anchored ? "rest" : "first", uv, ua, mc, ret);
 		fg->anchor_uah = div_s64(full * ret, 100);
 		fg->anchor_car = fg->car;
 		fg->anchored = true;
-- 
